<section class="about-section">
  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Why it's free</div>
    <h2 class="section-h">Two reasons.</h2>
    <div class="about-prose">
      <p>
        <strong>First,</strong> gated content doesn't build topic authority — it builds friction. The research I've done on how LinkedIn's 2026 algorithm treats credibility was clear about this. Readers who compound expertise over years do it in public, not behind email walls.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Second,</strong> this isn't a business model. I'm not trying to grow an audience to sell it something later. I write this because I test things in the lab that other recruiters would want to know about, and the cheapest way to share them is a public website.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
